From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkyWalker541 <178531074+SkyWalker541@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:10:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ChaOS: the Brick Pro's panel, a gh7003

The Brick Pro's panel reads 70 03 0a at 0xda-0xdc, which none of the
Brick's six panels do, so it got the jd9168's commands and a white
screen. TrimUI's Brick Pro U-Boot (tg4040 1.1.1) has a seventh panel for
it, gh7003, asked after the other six; this adds it, with their table.

---
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/brick_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/lcd/brick_panel.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /*
- * The TrimUI Brick's panel, which is one of six. TrimUI has built the Brick
+ * The TrimUI Brick's panel, which is one of six (seven, with the Brick
+ * Pro's: gh7003 below). TrimUI has built the Brick
  * with panels from different makers, each with its own controller, and their
  * U-Boot asks the panel which it is before sending it anything: it reads the
  * ID from DCS registers 0x04 and 0xda-0xdc, picks that controller's
@@ -525,6 +526,184 @@
  * were meant to be. Untested: no gc9702c Brick to try it on.
  */
 
